<title>GERMANY: GERMAN DATA THIS WEEK - Unemployment, trade.</title>
<headline>GERMAN DATA THIS WEEK - Unemployment, trade.</headline>
<dateline>BONN 1996-11-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following German economic indicators are expected to be released this week:</p>
<p>    INDICATOR	PERIOD	 PREVIOUS		 EXPECTED</p>
<p>					    DATA		     DATE</p>
<p> Unemployment	  Oct    3.991 million, 10.1 pct	Nov 7</p>
<p> Wholesale sales     Sept   -0.9 pct m/m, -2.0 y/y   Nov 7/8</p>
<p> Trade, c/a balance  Aug    +10.9 bln, -4.4 bln	Nov 8</p>
<p>NOTE - The previous unemployment data are September's pan-German seasonally adjusted total, and the unadjusted unemployment rate, as released by the Federal Labour Office.</p>
<p>The Federal Statistics Office said the expected release dates were targets.</p>
<p>-- Bonn newsroom, 49-228-26097150</p>
</text>
